cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PJM Cold-Spell Calibration Benchmark: When Cold-Spell Calibration Fails to Transfer"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-06
authors:
  - family-names: Goehner
    given-names: Dresden
    email: dresdengoehner@outlook.com
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Jurupa Valley, CA, USA"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DresdenGman/PJM-Cold-Calibration-Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Code, pre-registration, derived data and full results for a benchmark of
  probabilistic load forecasting across four PJM extreme-cold events
  (2014 polar vortex, 2015 anchor, 2017-18 cold snap, 2022 Winter Storm
  Elliott). Three forecaster families are combined with five conformal
  calibrators at day-ahead and one-hour horizons and judged under strictly
  chronological evaluation against retrospective leave-one-event-out
  transfer, under a protocol frozen before any result was computed.
keywords:
  - probabilistic load forecasting
  - conformal prediction
  - calibration transfer
  - extreme cold events
  - PJM
  - forecast evaluation
